//RS //! Private physical transport for compiler-implementation `Shared<T>` values.
//RS //!
//RS //! This is deliberately separate from the Source evaluator's logical
//RS //! `Shared(index)` carrier.  A value crossing the compiler entry/callback seam
//RS //! retains one physical root and performs typed payload conversion while the
//RS //! root's canonical read or edit permit is held.  The JIT and the generated
//RS //! NativeAdapter use this seam; no raw pointer, heap record sentinel, or
//RS //! evaluator session ID is a language value.
//RS 
